course: dictionary
lesson: 4789
title: Kind words for kind actions
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Humanely is an adverb. It tells you how something is done. It comes from the word human, and it means in a kind way, the way people should treat each other. «The animals were treated humanely at the shelter.» The word humanely tells you how they were treated: kindly and with care.
explain: Look at the words around it for clues. Humane is the adjective, and it means kind and caring. So humanely means in a kind way. A humane trap catches an animal without hurting it. Ask yourself: would "kindly" fit the sentence? If it still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
explain: Humanely means causing as little pain or suffering as possible. It is often used for animals or prisoners. «The rescuers caught the bird humanely» means they were careful and did not hurt it.
fact: Humanely means in a kind way that causes as little pain or suffering as possible.
fact: Humane is the adjective: a humane trap is one that catches animals without hurting them.
fact: «Treated humanely» means treated kindly, with care for how they feel.
fact: An adverb tells you how, where or when something happens, and humanely tells you how.
fact: A good check is to swap in "kindly" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «The wildlife helpers caught the fox humanely and let it go in the woods.» What does humanely tell us? | In a hurry, so the fox ran off | In a loud and noisy way | In a cross and angry way | *In a kind way, with as little harm as possible
exercise: Mia says a humane trap is a mean trap. What does humane mean? | Very big and heavy | Strong and made of metal | *Kind and caring, causing as little harm as possible | Angry with animals
exercise: «The puppy was treated humanely by the vet.» Find and copy the adverb. | puppy | vet | treated | *humanely
test: «The farmer moved the sheep humanely.» What does humanely mean here? | In a silly and funny way | In a fast and rushing way | *In a kind way, causing as little pain as possible | In a secret way
test: Which word is the adjective form of humanely? | *Humane | Human-shaped | Huge | Humanely
exam: «The scientists studied the frogs humanely, so they were not hurt.» Which word means the same as humanely here? | Loudly | Angrily | *Kindly | Cruelly
